  "narrative": "To improve measured education outcomes and maximize years of schooling, this policy proposes a coordinated suite of learner-centered interventions grounded in verified pedagogical evidence. Rather than relying on broad structural claims or untested writability assumptions, the strategy targets the instructional interface itself—where teaching practices, curricular content, and learning modalities directly influence student retention and progression. By modernizing how material is delivered, deepening the quality of classroom interaction, and strengthening foundational and advanced skill domains, the policy aims to reduce dropout risk and extend educational attainment.\n\nThe first pillar focuses on blended learning and teaching method reform. Blended learning integrates digital and face-to-face instruction, allowing learners to access flexible, self-paced materials while preserving the social and instructional benefits of classroom presence. Complementing this, a systematic shift in teaching methods toward evidence-based active learning, differentiated instruction, and formative assessment is designed to increase engagement and comprehension. Together, these interventions address both the delivery infrastructure and the pedagogical quality of daily instruction, targeting the moments when learners are most at risk of disengagement.\n\nThe second pillar supports domain-specific and foundational skill acquisition through enhanced STEM education and dialogic reading modalities. Expanding access to rigorous, inquiry-based STEM curricula improves academic success and signals long-term educational value to learners, encouraging continued enrollment. Simultaneously, dialogic reading interventions—structured, interactive story-based sessions—target early learners to build language comprehension and motivation at critical developmental stages. By anchoring early literacy in active conversation rather than passive reception, this modality establishes the foundational proficiency that predicts future schooling continuity.\n\nAll four interventions are presented as candidate-bound levers, explicitly avoiding claims of unverified authority or unsupported world-slot writability. Each is justified by its direct, evidence-backed pathway to sustained enrollment and learning, ensuring that no component is promoted beyond its established grounding. The combination is designed to be mutually reinforcing: early literacy and dialogic engagement foster readiness; improved teaching methods maintain quality; blended learning provides flexibility; and STEM enrichment supplies forward-looking academic motivation.",
  "interventions": [
    {
      "name": "Blended Learning Expansion",
